{"id": "EUVD-2026-86093", "enisaUuid": "a754f586-5c1d-3801-bea2-c148c584b324", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/amdkfd: Check bounds on allocate_doorbell\n\nallocated_doorbell has an option to set the doorbell id\nto a specific value (used by CRIU). This value was not\nbounds checked.\n\nCheck to confirm it's less than KFD_MAX_NUM_OF_QUEUES_PER_PROCESS.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:04:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-03T10:58:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7e06636260a2d95e3fa181bc337d0eeb812b7a41", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d2ddfc9b361b0d38c3ff4804ce42503e4bc97de", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e0cecd04a4fc4c75e375b91cf53eab5ba2e4ab7f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c2c89118c27cbd3adace62c5df19d15b0e96ade1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1f087bb8cf9e8797633da35c85435e557ef74d06"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97495", "GHSA-jwq7-cf4h-qr55"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0b5b9f22-6c5b-32ed-9221-1a94efc5dd51", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "1119e1a9-a8e1-36dc-89ea-ae938b50fc30", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "2c5a6e4b-a2d3-323e-8b23-6db60a9131bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "3b130b9f-bc19-38df-9e2e-5d9a73e071be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "6cfd70a9-6770-34cf-8602-fa1d6729c55c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5bb6a8fa75fcfda93592bee0a4910420ceab15f3 <c2c89118c27cbd3adace62c5df19d15b0e96ade1"}, {"id": "75af06ca-ca35-3250-9d3d-1ae3200e27bb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5bb6a8fa75fcfda93592bee0a4910420ceab15f3 <e0cecd04a4fc4c75e375b91cf53eab5ba2e4ab